.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 10, 2026" "Holberton School" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- simple Unix command interpreter project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Simple Shell is a Holberton School project whose purpose is to study how a
Unix command interpreter works and to implement a simple shell in C.

The project is developed progressively. Its final behavior is expected to
follow the project requirements and, unless otherwise specified, reproduce
the relevant behavior of
.BR /bin/sh .
.SH USAGE
When the shell executable is implemented, it will support the execution modes
required by the Holberton project.

In interactive mode, the shell reads commands from a terminal.

In non-interactive mode, commands may be supplied through standard input.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Exit status behavior will be documented as the implementation progresses and
is verified against the project requirements.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following examples describe the intended invocation of the completed
program:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
.fi
.PP
or:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi
.SH NOTES
This manual page is maintained alongside the implementation. Functionality is
documented as implemented and verified rather than assumed in advance.
